# The d special form: langlib original.
#
# The program prints now, then later, although later comes first in the
# source. `d<X> does not evaluate <X>; it returns a promise, and the
# promise is forced when it is applied, which happens only after the
# operand has printed now. Replace the d with an i and the output turns
# round, because then the operand is evaluated as usual.
``d``````.l.a.t.e.rri````.n.o.wri
